<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates lower on ample liquidity.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates lower on ample liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were largely softer on Tuesday, reflecting the ample liquidity in the system despite the remittance of tax payments to the government, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Some banks feel the market has enough liquidity to offset the tax payments,&quot; a trader said. &quot;Some are still long on pesos because they have prepared for the taxes.&quot;</p>
<p>Banks were estimated to have remitted to the government 18 to 25 billion pesos in income tax payments on Monday.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  APRIL 22		 APRIL 21</p>
<p>    1 W		9 11/16		 9  3/4</p>
<p>    2 W		9 11/16		 9  3/4</p>
<p>    1 M		9 13/16		 9  7/8</p>
<p>    2 M		9  7/8		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    3 M		9 15/16		 10</p>
<p>    6 M		10  3/16		10  1/4</p>
<p>    12M		10  7/16		10  7/16</p>
<p>    VAL		23-Apr		  22-Apr</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
